# Agent loader contract

Working-agreement bodies live in `.cursor/rules/` and `.cursor/skills/`.
Project memories live in `.cursor/memory/`. Claude Code loads those same
files through `@` imports in `CLAUDE.md` (and skill directory symlinks).

Do not:

- run `claude /init` or `/import` in this repo (they copy text into `CLAUDE.md`)
- inline rule text into `CLAUDE.md` or `AGENTS.md`
- generate `CLAUDE.md` from the rules
- create `.agents/` or a generator that emits `.mdc` files
- symlink `CLAUDE.md` to `AGENTS.md` (`AGENTS.md` is an index, not the rules)

`tests/agent-loader-lockstep.test.ts` fails the PR if any of those happen.
Edit a `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` file to change a rule. Add a matching `@`
line in `CLAUDE.md` for a new always-on rule.
